    "body": "D2 [BLACK] — TEXTURE SCALE/MATERIAL CYCLE STATUS\n\nFresh authority re-read completed:\n- current main = `b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`\n- current branch HEAD = `2b0438cb817d41e53bec23944af7237893e12b4b`\n- #199 ACTIVE visual/texture law re-read\n- #206 Night School law re-read\n- current Constitution re-read before terminal status\n- OWNER OSS-only override remains active\n\nAdditional existing-source OSS probe:\n\nBLACK CLOTH\n- C00-A close black-shirt local patch: entropy `0.436512`, Canny occupancy `0.0490000`, fine residual mean `0.0114693`\n- C00-C master/full local black-shirt patch: entropy `0.398654`, Canny occupancy `0.0644444`, fine residual mean `0.00673602`\n\nDirectional result: fine residual falls by about 41% between the close/detail and master/full probes even though hard-edge occupancy does not fall monotonically. This again supports separating structural edges from microtexture/noise.\n\nCombined with the prior same-cycle probes:\n- calm ivory cloth: strong fine-detail collapse with scale;\n- black cloth: fine-detail collapse while essential structural edges may remain;\n- leather: selected specular/high-contrast structure survives more strongly than calm cloth microtexture;\n- neon/key-visual skin: ~2x base Canny occupancy and ~39% higher fine residual in the tested local patches;\n- neon/key-visual ivory: ~56% higher fine residual and ~46% higher entropy even though Canny occupancy is lower, proving edge density alone cannot represent texture density.\n\nLEARNING STATE\n\n`TEXTURE_SCALE_MODEL_R01 = PARTIAL / VERIFIED SUPPORTING SIGNAL`\n\nSupported model:\n`TEXTURE = SCALE_BUDGET x MATERIAL_RESPONSE`\n\nSupported production direction:\n- CLOSE = macro + meso + sparse selected micro;\n- MID = macro + material-defining meso; most micro collapses;\n- FULL/FAR = macro + structural edges + identity-critical accents;\n- calm cloth spends less fine-frequency budget with distance;\n- specular materials may retain sparse high-contrast material cues;\n- hard-edge density and fine/noise density must remain separate QC signals.\n\nNOT CLAIMED:\n- `TEXTURE_LANGUAGE_R01 = PASS`\n- material-semantic numeric envelopes\n- canon lock\n- production activation\n- model-weight training\n\nBLOCKER:\n`PER_MATERIAL_SEMANTIC_NUMERIC_QC = OSS_CAPABILITY_NOT_AVAILABLE / CUSTOM_CODE_FORBIDDEN`\n\nReason: the only physically available mature OSS image-analysis CLI in the current runtime is ImageMagick 7.1.2-1. It provides native statistics, Canny, blur/difference and other image operators, but no direct semantic understanding of skin/hair/ivory cloth/black cloth/leather/metal. G'MIC/Krita/OpenToonz/OpenImageIO are not installed in the current runtime. A custom extractor/wrapper is forbidden by OWNER.\n\nNEXT LEGAL ACTION:\ncontinue existing-source OSS-only transfer analysis and material routing; do not write code and do not generate/edit images.",
