    "body": "ZORR MODE\n\nTYPE = DUNCAN SANDBOX / DRAWING QC EXPERIMENT\nSTATUS = DRAW_QC_R02_PASS\nPRODUCTION_MUTATION = NO\nCANON_MUTATION = NO\nMERGE_AUTHORIZED = NO\n\n## EXACT BASE / HEAD\nBASE_MAIN_OBSERVED = b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1\nHEAD = 341cb2a62990295eeef71f9c9ea0765c4b104c3a\nBRANCH = duncan3/zorr-draw-qc-r01\n\nAuthority: #199 character drawing law; #201 visual taboo; #206 hard open-code law.\n\n## OPEN CODE REUSED\nMinimal glue around pinned open-source stack already present on this branch:\n- numpy==2.3.5\n- opencv-python-headless==4.14.0.94\n- checkout action pinned by commit\n\nNo custom framework introduced.\n\n## R01 ABSOLUTE ANCHOR QC\nExisting R01 remains intact:\n- 4..6 dominant tone bands\n- strong-edge density 0.08..0.14\n- deep ink <0.05 in the intended face/skin measurement domain\n- line hierarchy ratio >=4.0\n- high-frequency Laplacian variance <=800\n\nR01 absolute thresholds are not weakened by R02.\n\n## R02 SEMANTIC REGION QC\nFresh audit found that whole-component measurement can mix face/skin with Character Truth black masses such as hair, shirt, and accessories.\n\nImplemented:\n- legacy analyze_image_bgr() retained;\n- analyze_region_bgr(image, region_mask) added;\n- semantic identity mask is supplied upstream, not inferred from color in QC;\n- empty/mismatched masks fail closed.\n\nSemantic-region GREEN evidence:\n- HEAD 29917478de99fd74a9ac5c6de9467f0bf57976bd\n- zorr-draw-qc-r01 run 33319255481 = SUCCESS\n- hq-validate run 33319255493 = SUCCESS\n- oss-security run 33319255489 = SUCCESS\n\n## R02 MODEL-SHEET TRANSFER QC\nAbsolute anchor QC and cross-view transfer QC are separate domains.\n\nCurrent C00-B three-view front/3/4 study dispersion:\n- tone range = 1.0\n- edge CV = 0.0453568777\n- deep-ink CV = 0.0904618353\n- line-hierarchy CV = 0.0421699512\n- high-frequency CV = 0.2598974183\n\nProvisional transfer envelope:\n- minimum views = 3\n- tone range <=1.0\n- edge CV <=0.06\n- deep-ink CV <=0.12\n- line-hierarchy CV <=0.06\n- high-frequency CV <=0.30\n\nControlled one-view drift fixture fails all five transfer drift gates as expected.\n\nImplementation GREEN parent:\n- HEAD 822fd472d907514f4a1cc5c5fa0ce5d36ad71d12\n- zorr-draw-qc-r01 run 33319347422 = SUCCESS\n- hq-validate run 33319347462 = SUCCESS\n- oss-security job in run 33319347431 = SUCCESS\n\n## FINAL FRESH EVIDENCE HEAD\nHEAD = 341cb2a62990295eeef71f9c9ea0765c4b104c3a\n\n- zorr-draw-qc-r01 run 33319380232 = SUCCESS\n- hq-validate run 33319380231 = SUCCESS\n- oss-security run 33319380228 = SUCCESS\n\nEvidence file:\nexperiments/draw_qc_r01/R02_TRANSFER_QC_EVIDENCE.md\n\n## CURRENT VERDICT\nSEMANTIC_REGION_QC = PASS\nMODEL_SHEET_TRANSFER_QC = PASS\nABSOLUTE_R01_AND_TRANSFER_R02_DOMAIN_SEPARATION = PASS\nDRAW_QC_R02 = PASS\n\nPRODUCTION_STYLE_CANON = NOT CLAIMED\nMERGE_AUTHORIZED = NO\nNEXT = R03 HEAD_GEOMETRY_CONSISTENCY\n\nNo claim is made that model weights were trained or that production/canon state was promoted by this sandbox PR.",
